== VERDICT (REFUTE lens) ==
PROV-21 claim: `--version -Z` prints the banner and exits 0; "the unknown option is never reported".
MEASUREMENT: REAL. Reproduces on the current binaries (A1-A3), whose sha256 equal the README's; no cpp/ source is
  newer than the binaries and `git diff 1151b22..HEAD -- cpp/` is empty, so the binary is not stale. Not a shell
  artefact: the reproducer is bash with quoted argv and file-captured rc. Not escape-dependent: no data is read before
  the version gate (the other verifier's `env -u EA_ALLOW_SHORT_DATASET` runs agree).
DEFECT CLAIM: REFUTED -- it is the documented, intended rule, stated in four places, none quoted by expected.txt:
  1. cpp/shared/TestRunUtils.h:316-317  "Whichever comes FIRST decides: a "--version", an unrecognised option, or the
     "--" separator."  (expected.txt quotes only the sentence AFTER this one.)
  2. commit b63aff1 (F04 repair) message: "Whichever comes first -- a --version or an unrecognised option -- decides."
  3. audits/2026-10-11-independent-audit/ORCHESTRATOR-CHECKS.md OC-80 (~l.7217-7227): "A legitimate --version request
     contains no invalid options, so this costs nothing: whichever comes first ... decides."
  4. cpp/selftest/regression-option-order.sh:177-179 (comment to the `-Z --version` pair test).
  And the analysis phase itself (logs/analysis/cli-build.md:132) filed `version-then-Z rc=0` under "documented option".
ATTRIBUTION WRONG: -Z is not the cause. B1-B6 + C3: `--version -q`, `--version <file> 8`, `--version -Z <file> 8`,
  `--version --bogus`, `-q --version -Z`, `--version -- -Z` all -> banner, rc 0. A leading --version IS the request;
  everything after it is not parsed. That is also GNU coreutils' convention on this host (E1-E5, E10-E11:
  `gls --version --bogus` rc 0 vs `gls --bogus --version` rc 2) and bash's (E6). python3/git/gawk differ (E7-E9) --
  the convention is not universal, but the fork chose and documented the coreutils one.
F04 CLASS DOES NOT APPLY: OC-80 defines it as "the operator supplied operands, so they asked for an assessment and got
  success with nothing done". `--version -Z` has no operand, no -o, no report path; D shows no file is created.
  The README itself concedes "the operator did ask for the version" and "Harmless in intent".
DIRECTION: neutral. No figure, no report, no write. Severity by brief: NOT-A-DEFECT (not even LOW).
NOT PINNED: no regression asserts `--version -Z` -> 0 (only `--version` alone -> 0, `-Z --version` -> fail, and a
  late --version -> refused). The rule is documented, not tested; that is a test-coverage note, not a defect.

== ADJACENT CANDIDATE, NOT PROV-21 (hand to the orchestrator for its own ID) ==
The documented rule "whichever comes first decides" is implemented for the SHORT unknown spelling only.
scanArgs (TestRunUtils.h:185-188) treats every `--long` element as "a long option" and `continue`s without setting
rejectAt, so an unknown LONG option BEFORE --version does not decide:
  F1-F3  `--bogus --version` (and `--version-x --version`)  -> rc 0, banner, all three tools
  F4     `--bogus` alone                                      -> rc 255, "illegal option -- -" (getopt rejects it)
  C1/F6  `-Z --version [...]`                                 -> rc 255 (the short spelling obeys the rule)
  F5     `--bogus --version <file> 8`                         -> rc 0, banner, NOTHING ASSESSED, operands present
  G1     `--bogus -o G_stale.json --version <file> 8`         -> rc 0, banner, pre-existing G_stale.json UNCHANGED:
         exit 0 beside a stale report -- the A04/F04/C14 shape OC-80 repaired for `-Z` ("the same class, through an
         invalid option"), open through the long spelling. The b63aff1 controls exercised `-Z` only.
  G2     control, `-Z -o G_stale2.json --version <file> 8`    -> rc 255, file unchanged (OC-51's documented
         "argument-parse failures above the claim" member: nonzero exit, consumer not misled).
Direction neutral (no figure). Brief scale: LOW (exit-status-channel fail-open, no report written; the repo rated the
identical `-Z` shape a repairable defect, F04). Needs no data, no escape. Darwin arm64 only; the mechanism is in the
prescan, not in getopt, so platform-independent by construction but NOT measured elsewhere.
